---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ServiceCard from '../../components/ServiceCard.astro';
import CTABlock from '../../components/CTABlock.astro';

const related = [
  { title: 'Septic Install & Repairs', description: 'DEQ certified installation and repair of septic systems.', href: '/services/septic-install-repairs' },
  { title: 'Septic Installation Cost in Oregon', description: 'What a new septic system actually costs and why.', href: '/resources/septic-installation-cost-oregon' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Oregon Septic Basics | D&D Land Works"
	description="How Oregon DEQ regulates septic systems in Lane County: soil testing, permitting, system types, and what property owners need to know."
>
	<Hero
		eyebrow="Informational"
		headline="Oregon Septic Basics"
		subheadline="If your property isn't on city sewer, DEQ decides what kind of septic system you're allowed to have, and it starts with a soil test."
		primaryCta={{ label: 'Call 541-401-8726', href: 'tel:5414018726' }}
		secondaryCta={{ label: 'Free Estimate', href: '/contact' }}
	/>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16">
		<h2 class="font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-3xl text-ink">
			It Starts With a Soil Test
		</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
			Before any septic system gets designed in Oregon, the soil gets tested. A percolation test
			measures how fast water moves through the ground, and that result determines the drainfield
			size and type DEQ will approve. Sandy soil near the coast often percs fast and needs less
			drainfield area. Clay-heavy ground common around Eugene percs slower and can require a bigger
			field, or in tougher cases, an alternative system engineered specifically for that soil.
		</p>
		<h2 class="mt-12 font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-3xl text-ink">
			Who Signs Off on What
		</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
			Lane County's sanitarian reviews the site evaluation and issues the permit. DEQ sets the
			statewide standards the system has to meet. Only a DEQ-certified installer can legally put the
			system in the ground once the permit is issued, which is a separate credential from a general
			contractor license.
		</p>
		<h2 class="mt-12 font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-3xl text-ink">
			Standard vs. Alternative Systems
		</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
			A standard gravity drainfield works where soil and slope cooperate. Where they don't, poor
			percolation, a high water table, or a lot too small for a standard field, Oregon allows
			alternative systems engineered around the specific limitation. Which one a property qualifies
			for comes down entirely to what the soil test shows, not preference.
		</p>
		<h2 class="mt-12 font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-3xl text-ink">
			Buying or Selling a Property on Septic
		</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
			Oregon requires a septic evaluation report in most property sales where the system predates
			certain regulatory changes, separate from the install and repair work D&D Land Works handles.
			If that evaluation turns up a failing drainfield or an undersized tank, that's where a
			DEQ-certified installer comes in to fix it.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
			D&D Land Works is licensed and bonded under CCB #261742 and DEQ certified for septic install
			and repair, serving Eugene, Springfield, and the rest of <a href="/service-area" class="text-brand-blue underline hover:text-brand-blue-dark">Lane County</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-16">
		<h2 class="font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-2xl text-ink text-center">
			Related
		</h2>
		<div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
			{related.map((item) => <ServiceCard title={item.title} description={item.description} href={item.href} />)}
		</div>
	</section>
	<CTABlock
		headline="Get Your System Checked"
		subheadline="Free estimate for septic install or repair anywhere in Lane County."
	/>
</BaseLayout>
